# Requests for testing the API with the REST Client extension in VS Code.
# Click "Send Request" above any request (or put the cursor in it and press Ctrl+Alt+R / Cmd+Alt+R).
# Requests are separated by lines starting with ###.

# Where the app is running. Swap these two lines to test the deployed version.
@host = http://localhost:3000
# @host = https://YOUR-PROJECT.vercel.app


### The usage message
GET {{host}}/


### Read a key. On a fresh database this is a 404: nothing is stored yet.
GET {{host}}/api/greeting


### Store a value under that key. Run this, then run the GET above again.
PUT {{host}}/api/greeting
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "value": "hello from DES222"
}


### Overwrite it with something else, then GET again.
PUT {{host}}/api/greeting
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "value": "a different greeting"
}


### The value doesn't have to be a string. Any JSON works: numbers, lists, objects.
PUT {{host}}/api/profile
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "value": {
    "name": "Ann",
    "score": 42,
    "tags": ["student", "des222"]
  }
}


### And it comes back as the same JSON.
GET {{host}}/api/profile


### A key that was never stored → 404 with an error message.
GET {{host}}/api/nothing-here


### A PUT with no body → 400. The API tells you what it expected.
PUT {{host}}/api/greeting


### A PUT whose body isn't { "value": … } → also 400.
PUT {{host}}/api/greeting
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "greeting": "this is the wrong shape"
}
